# openkobo hardened sshd_config.
# Replaces the stock config, which allowed empty-password root login
# (PermitRootLogin yes / PermitEmptyPasswords yes). Root login here is
# key-only, and the host keys are the device-unique ones that
# /etc/init.d/ssh stages in tmpfs at boot (never the keys shared by every
# stock Kobo).

Protocol 2

HostKey /tmp/openkobo/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key
HostKey /tmp/openkobo/ssh/ssh_host_rsa_key

PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
PubkeyAuthentication yes
PasswordAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
ChallengeResponseAuthentication no

AuthorizedKeysFile /tmp/openkobo/authorized_keys
AllowUsers root

AllowTcpForwarding no
X11Forwarding no
PermitTunnel no

ClientAliveInterval 15
ClientAliveCountMax 4
Compression no

Subsystem sftp internal-sftp
